WEBVTT
Kind: subtitles
Language: en

1
00:00.200 --> 00:04.400
So the Problem Statement Worksheet is an approach that we use

2
00:04.400 --> 00:08.070
to make sure that the definition of the problem is as good as it can be.

3
00:08.450 --> 00:11.910
It starts with asking: what is the problem we're trying to solve?

4
00:12.260 --> 00:17.600
And there we're applying the SMART framework to ensure
that definition is as clear and concise as possible,

5
00:17.600 --> 00:21.200
and everybody's aligned on that definition.

6
00:21.200 --> 00:23.910
It then has a number of other components, where

7
00:24.290 --> 00:27.970
it asks us to consider: what is the context of the problem?

8
00:28.490 --> 00:32.200
What is the scope of the solution set?
What are the constraints that we need to solve for?

9
00:32.200 --> 00:35.600
Who are all the stakeholders we need to think through?

10
00:35.600 --> 00:39.200
And ultimately, how are we going to measure
the success of solving this problem?

11
00:39.200 --> 00:42.780
And the benefit of using the Problem Statement Worksheet
is that it's a great way

12
00:42.920 --> 00:47.800
to drive alignment and ensure everyone is aligned
on what the problem we're trying to solve is,

13
00:47.800 --> 00:50.400
and we've really nailed the definition of the problem.

14
00:50.400 --> 00:52.870
So why do we use these components
in the Problem Statement Worksheet?

15
00:53.190 --> 00:56.200
Well, it enables us to do a number of different things.

16
00:56.200 --> 01:01.600
It enables us to think about how we can best align everyone on this problem —
both the people directly involved in the problem-solving process,

17
01:01.600 --> 01:05.400
as well as the wider set of stakeholders.

18
01:05.400 --> 01:08.030
It also enables us to be creative,

19
01:08.260 --> 01:13.400
and to think around what all the options are that we should be considering,
and what is in scope,

20
01:13.400 --> 01:18.720
and ensure that all the different sources of insight
are fully thought through from the beginning of the process.

21
01:19.270 --> 01:22.600
And it also has an element of making sure we're practical.

22
01:22.600 --> 01:28.200
And so as we think about what success looks like,
as we think about the constraints that we're facing,

23
01:28.200 --> 01:33.660
it then enables us to be more precise
when we get to the structuring and prioritisation

24
01:33.830 --> 01:37.400
steps of the hypothesis-led approach, to get there more efficiently.

25
01:37.400 --> 01:42.800
So the Problem Statement Worksheet enables you
to both broaden the solution set —

26
01:42.800 --> 01:48.350
and think about: have you thought about the full scope
and all the different stakeholders that need to be involved —

27
01:48.520 --> 01:52.600
while at the same time ensuring that it's practical,

28
01:52.600 --> 01:56.800
and you've thought about the different constraints you need to solve for
in order to deliver the impact and meet the criteria for success.
